    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d74">

                <pb facs="0159" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1865p3/pg77"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr.
                        Sanford</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 167.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 8, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your despatch of the 20th of March, No.
                    250, has just been received. The subject to which it relates is an important
                    one, and the suggestions you have <pb facs="0160" n="78" xml:id="pg78"/> offered
                    are valuable. I have submitted the despatch for perusal to the Secretary of the
                    Treasury.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry S. Sanford,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., Brussels.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
